From: Codex local A376B compatibility adaptation
Subject: [PATCH] Keep AZH4 package blocklist behavior in M2

Reason: mods2-preflight.txt:75,136 shows the fork's legacy blocklist patch fails
against AZH4 PackageBlockListPolicy and PmLifecycleImpl. The old patch replaces
LDU state and deletes lifecycle observers. Keep donor PackageManager behavior
for this exact M2 profile until an AZH4 port can preserve its policy contract.
Files: scripts/internal/apply_modules.sh.
Verification: M2-only module dispatch fixture, non-M2 unchanged fixture, module
preflight, shell syntax and sequential patch replay. Optional legacy UN1CA
blocklist customization is absent on M2. Revert0056.

---
--- a/scripts/internal/apply_modules.sh
+++ b/scripts/internal/apply_modules.sh
@@ -13,6 +13,15 @@ APPLY_MODULE()
     local MODNAME
     local MODAUTH
 
+    # AZH4 changed the PackageBlockListPolicy and its lifecycle wiring. The
+    # fork's legacy blocklist patch removes that donor behavior, so retain the
+    # donor implementation for this M2 profile until an exact port is reviewed.
+    if [ "${ROM_SOURCE_CONFIG:-}" = "essi_a376b_android16" ] && \
+            [[ "$MODPATH" == */mods/blocklist ]]; then
+        LOGW "Skipping optional legacy Package Blocklist mod for A376B Android 16; AZH4 policy layout differs"
+        return 0
+    fi
+
     if [ ! -d "$MODPATH" ]; then
